Assembler Version 06
====================
Assembled by: version 05

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
Same feature set as version 05, refactored with hash tables:

Syntax:
- Non-standard (custom) mnemonic syntax: LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, STAZ(),Y, etc.
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Quoted strings with \n escape: "text" and "\n"
- Label definitions (at start of line) with PC value or explicit assignment: label = $xxxx
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx
- Low byte operator: <label
- High byte operator: >label
- Relative branch operator: ~label (used for branch targets)
- Labels as 2-byte operands (absolute addresses)
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly (pass 1 collects labels, pass 2 resolves and emits)

Instruction set (non-standard mnemonics):
- ADC#, ADCZ, AND#, ASLA
- BCC, BCS, BEQ, BITZ, BMI, BNE, BPL, BRK
- CLC, CMP#, CMP,Y
- EORZ
- INCZ, INX, INY
- JMP, JSR
- LDA#, LDAZ(),Y, LDA,X, LDA,Y, LDAZ, LDAZ,X, LDX#, LDY#
- LSRA
- ORAZ
- PHA, PLA
- RTS
- SBC#, SBCZ, SEC
- STA, STAZ(),Y, STA,X, STA,Y, STAZ, STAZ,X
- TAY, TYA

Error handling:
- Label not found (error 1)
- Duplicate label (error 2)
- Opcode not found (error 3)
- Expected hex value (error 4)

New in this version (relative to version 05):
- Hash table-based lookup for both labels and instructions (replacing linear table scan)
- Scramble table for hash computation
- Heap-based storage for hash table entries
- Separate label and instruction hash tables (256-entry each)
- PHA/PLA used for saving/restoring next character (instead of NEXTCHAR variable)

